+# ATTACK — red team vs `parseCsvLine` (src/csv.mjs)
+
+Target: `parseCsvLine` / `CsvError` in `src/csv.mjs` against the contract in
+`README.md`. Everything below was actually executed with Node v25.2.1 from the
+project root. No failing trace was found; `traces/` was therefore not created.
+
+Verdict: **pass**.
+
+## Method
+
+1. Read README.md sentence by sentence and wrote an independent character-by-
+   character oracle (state machine: start / unquoted / quoted / after-quote,
+   terminator stripped first) from the text alone, without looking at the
+   test file's reference implementation.
+2. Read `src/csv.mjs` looking for divergence points: the `end` computation
+   for the trailing terminator, the unbounded `indexOf('"', j)` in the quoted
+   path, the `q + 1 < end` escaped-quote look-ahead, the `j === end` return
+   paths, and the two `for (;;)` loops (hang risk).
+3. Ran the attacks below. `npm test` (21 tests) passes as a baseline.
+
+## Attack classes and results
+
+### Exhaustive grammar enumeration (held)
+Every string of length 0..7 over the alphabet `"`, `,`, `\n`, `\r`, `a`, ` `
+(335,923 strings) compared with the oracle: 0 mismatches. Both the
+returned arrays and the throw/no-throw decision agree; every thrown error
+is a `CsvError` with `name === "CsvError"` and an integer `position` in
+`[0, text.length]`.
+
+### Random fuzz over a hostile alphabet (held)
+300,000 random strings, length 0..29, drawn from `"` (double weight), `,`,
+`\n`, `\r`, `\r\n`, `a`, `b`, `\t`, `\0`, lone high surrogate U+D800, lone
+low surrogate U+DC00, U+1F600, BOM U+FEFF, U+2028, NEL U+0085, NBSP U+00A0:
+0 mismatches against the oracle, and nothing but `CsvError` was thrown.
+
+### Line-terminator handling (held)
+- `\n`, `\r\n` alone -> `[""]`; `a\n`, `a\r\n`, `a,\n`, `,\r\n`, `"a",\n` OK.
+- Lone `\r` (`\r`, `a\r`, `a,b\r`, `"a"\r`) -> CsvError, as README says.
+- Multiple trailing terminators (`\n\n`, `\r\r\n`, `\r\n\r\n`, `a\n\r\n`,
+  `a,b\r\n\n`, `a,b\n\r`) -> CsvError.
+- Terminator not at the end (`"a"\n,`, `"a"\n"`, `a\nb`) -> CsvError.
+- Terminators inside quotes (`"\r"`, `"a\rb"`, `"a\r\n"\r\n`, `"\n"\r\n`,
+  `"\r\n"\n`, `"a""\n"`) are literal and the trailing terminator is still
+  stripped. `"a\n` / `"a\r\n` (quote never closes, text ends in terminator)
+  -> CsvError, not a silently swallowed terminator.
+- U+2028, U+0085, U+FEFF are not treated as terminators (literal in fields;
+  CsvError after a closing quote).
+
+### Quote handling (held)
+`""` -> `[""]`; `"",` -> `["",""]`; `""""` -> `['"']`; `"""` -> CsvError
+(unterminated); `""" "` -> `['" ']`; `" ""` -> CsvError; `"a"b`, `"a" `,
+`"a"` + NBSP/U+2028/U+FEFF -> CsvError with position at the offending
+character; ` "a"`, `a"b`, `a "b"` -> CsvError; `"a",""",` -> CsvError
+(unterminated field starting at 4). README examples reproduce exactly.
+
+### Empty inputs / empty fields (held)
+`""` -> `[""]`, `,` -> `["",""]`, `,,` -> `["","",""]`, `a,` -> `["a",""]`.
+
+### Error type / shape (held)
+Thrown value: `instanceof CsvError` and `instanceof Error`, prototype chain
+`CsvError.prototype -> Error.prototype`, own `name === "CsvError"`,
+`String(e)` = `CsvError: ...`, non-empty message, integer `position`.
+Both `CsvError` and `parseCsvLine` are exported (`Object.keys(mod)`).
+Minor non-contract note: `CsvError.prototype.name` is the inherited
+`"Error"`; only instances carry `"CsvError"`. README does not speak to
+this, so no trace.
+
+### Non-string inputs (held; README says TypeError)
+`undefined`, missing argument, `null`, `0`, `1`, `NaN`, `true`, `Symbol`,
+`10n`, `{}`, `[]`, `["a"]`, function, `{toString}`, `Object.create(null)`,
+`Proxy` of object and of function all throw `TypeError` and not `CsvError`.
+`new String("a,b")` also throws `TypeError`. README's "not a string" is
+arguably ambiguous for String wrapper objects; the implementation documents
+"primitive string" and `typeof` agrees, so this was judged a legitimate
+reading, not a violation. Extra arguments are ignored.
+
+### Return shape (held)
+Plain `Array` (`Array.isArray`, prototype is `Array.prototype`, own props
+only indices + `length`, not frozen), every element a primitive string, a
+fresh array per call.
+
+### Unicode (held)
+BOM kept as first character of field 1; lone surrogates U+D800 / U+DC00
+survive in both quoted and unquoted fields and in either order; non-BMP,
+NBSP, U+2028, NEL are literal.
+
+### Performance / hang (held)
+Timed with `performance.now()` around the single call, cold, for 100 KB,
+1 MB and 10 MB of each shape: all quotes (unterminated), all escaped quotes
+in one field, `"",` repeated, `"a",` repeated, `a""` alternating, all commas,
+all `x`, quoted `x`, quoted CRLFs, quoted commas, error at the very end,
+error at the start, unterminated with many escapes, emoji, lone surrogates,
+100 KB of `\n` inside quotes, `"\n",` repeated, char after closing quote at
+the end.
+
+Worst 100 KB case: 6.5 ms (all commas). Worst 1 MB: 18.6 ms. Worst 10 MB:
+270.7 ms. The 5-million-escaped-quote 10 MB field also flattens and compares
+equal to the expected content in 22 ms (checked because the quoted path
+builds the field with `+=`). Nothing is super-linear; no hang.
+
+## Code-level observations (not violations)
+- `indexOf('"', j)` is not bounded by `end`, but the stripped tail is only
+  `\n` or `\r\n`, which cannot contain a quote, so `q >= end` is unreachable
+  and the `q === -1` branch covers every unterminated case.
+- A `\r` directly before the trailing `\n` is consumed as part of the
+  terminator even if it is "inside" an unterminated quote (`"a\r\n`); the
+  result is still the required CsvError because the quote never closes.
+
+## What broke
+Nothing. No trace written.
