+# Changes
+
+## Round 0 — no traces yet; hardened against contract lines
+
+`traces/` does not exist yet, so this round works from README.md alone.
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+Rewrote `parseCsvLine` as a single index-based linear scan (the previous
+version toggled a `quoted` flag on every `"`, enforced none of the error rules,
+and was O(n²) via `rest.slice(1)`).
+
+Contract lines now enforced, each with tests:
+
+- **Non-string input throws `TypeError`** — `typeof text !== "string"`, so
+  `String` objects, `toString`/`Symbol.toPrimitive` tricks, `undefined`,
+  `Symbol`, `BigInt`, arrays, Buffers etc. are all rejected. The message is a
+  constant, so building it can never throw something else.
+- **Returns `string[]` or throws `CsvError`, nothing else** — every error path
+  throws `CsvError`; no other exception can arise from a string input. Fuzzed
+  (20 000 random strings) and exhaustively checked (all strings up to length 5
+  over `" , \n \r a`) against an independent reference state machine.
+- **`CsvError` is an exported `Error` subclass** — `name === "CsvError"`, plus a
+  `position` (zero-based index of the offending character) for diagnostics.
+- **Never hangs; 100 KB within a second** — one pass, `indexOf`/`slice` based,
+  no regex backtracking. 100 KB pathological inputs (all commas, all escaped
+  quotes, all quoted `\r\n`, unterminated, error at end) parse in ~1–10 ms;
+  10 MB in < 300 ms. Tested with a 1 s ceiling on 16 shapes plus a 1 MB case.
+- **`,` separates fields; `""` → `[""]`; `a,` → `["a", ""]`** — including
+  `,` → `["", ""]`, leading/trailing/consecutive commas.
+- **Quoted fields; `""` is one `"`; commas, `\n`, `\r\n` (and lone `\r`) are
+  literal inside quotes** — including escaped quotes at the start/end of a
+  field, `""""` → `['"']`, and escaped quote directly before the terminator.
+- **After a closing quote only `,`, the record terminator or end of text may
+  follow** — space, tab, any other char, a lone `\r`, a second terminator, or
+  a terminator followed by more text are all `CsvError`.
+- **A quoted field that never closes is a `CsvError`** — including when the
+  text ends with a terminator inside the quotes (`"a\n`, `"a\r\n`).
+- **Outside quotes a `"` anywhere is a `CsvError`** — `a"b`, `a "b"`, ` "a"`,
+  `a,b"`, `a""`, etc.
+- **Whitespace outside quotes is part of the field** — spaces, tabs, NBSP,
+  `\v`, `\f` all kept; nothing is trimmed.
+- **One terminator (`\n` or `\r\n`) at the very end is removed; any other
+  unquoted `\r`/`\n` is a `CsvError`** — `a\r` (lone CR), `a\n\n`, `\n\r\n`,
+  `a\r\r\n`, `a\nb`, `\na` are all errors; `\n` → `[""]`, `\r\n` → `[""]`.
+- **Every other character is literal** — NUL, C0/C1 controls, ESC sequences,
+  BOM (not stripped), ` `/` `/`\u0085` (not terminators), other
+  Unicode quote/comma look-alikes, non-BMP, combining marks, ZWJ sequences, and
+  lone surrogates (preserved as-is because scanning is by UTF-16 code unit).
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+Expanded from 4 tests to 21: one section per contract line above, a
+result-shape test (fresh `Array` of primitive strings), timing tests, a
+serialize→parse round-trip fuzz, a "nothing but `CsvError`" fuzz, and an
+exhaustive comparison against a reference state machine on short strings.
+
+### Traces fixed
+
+None (round 0, no traces).
